
SETQUOT(8)          UNIX Programmer's Manual           SETQUOT(8)

NAME
     setquot - make block quota on a directory

SYNOPSIS
     setquot directory [ current ] maximum

DESCRIPTION
     _S_e_t_q_u_o_t sets up or modifies the maximum block quota and
     present block count for a directory by modifying the file
     _d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_y/._q.  If _c_u_r_r_e_n_t is not specified, the current
     usage count is unchanged.  Group masters may change the quo-
     tas of users in their group.  Otherwise, _s_e_t_q_u_o_t requires
     super-user privileges.

FILES
     _d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_y/.q        quota node for _d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_y

SEE ALSO
     file(1), ls(1), pq(1), quota(2), qstat(2)

BUGS
     _M_a_x_i_m_u_m is an absolute maximum.  Hence programs that write
     in _d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_y may fail if intermediate usage exceeds the
     quota.

